Dear Dani,

read the red stuff, especially the second sentence. You probably try to squeeze out too many estimates from not enough information. How many sites and how many repeated measurements per site do you have ?

Have you tried building up your model step by step, starting with a simple models with few covariates and then adding in more and more ? You can then use estimates of the simpler models as initial values for the next step in the progression from simple to complex model.

Best regards --- Marc

